gfs2: Use wait_event_freezable_timeout() for freezable kthread

jira KERNEL-1773
Rebuild_History Non-Buildable kernel-4.18.0-553.176.1.el8_10
commit-author Kevin Hao <haokexin@gmail.com>
commit edd13270fa0660fda608b5f2bf989c770d90d469
Empty-Commit: Cherry-Pick Conflicts during history rebuild.
Will be included in final tarball splat. Ref for failed cherry-pick at:
ciq/ciq_backports/kernel-4.18.0-553.176.1.el8_10/edd13270.failed

A freezable kernel thread can enter frozen state during freezing by
either calling try_to_freeze() or using wait_event_freezable() and its
variants. So for the following snippet of code in a kernel thread loop:
  try_to_freeze();
  wait_event_interruptible_timeout();

We can change it to a simple wait_event_freezable_timeout() and then
eliminate a function call.

	Signed-off-by: Kevin Hao <haokexin@gmail.com>
	Signed-off-by: Andreas Gruenbacher <agruenba@redhat.com>
(cherry picked from commit edd13270fa0660fda608b5f2bf989c770d90d469)
	Signed-off-by: Jonathan Maple <jmaple@ciq.com>

# Conflicts:
#	fs/gfs2/log.c
diff --cc fs/gfs2/log.c
index ff85ca4c67fc,6b3ba8f7b67a..000000000000
--- a/fs/gfs2/log.c
+++ b/fs/gfs2/log.c
@@@ -1326,9 -1337,8 +1326,14 @@@ int gfs2_logd(void *data
  
  		t = gfs2_tune_get(sdp, gt_logd_secs) * HZ;
  
++<<<<<<< HEAD
 +		try_to_freeze();
 +
 +		t = wait_event_interruptible_timeout(sdp->sd_logd_waitq,
++=======
+ 		t = wait_event_freezable_timeout(sdp->sd_logd_waitq,
+ 				test_bit(SDF_FORCE_AIL_FLUSH, &sdp->sd_flags) ||
++>>>>>>> edd13270fa06 (gfs2: Use wait_event_freezable_timeout() for freezable kthread)
  				gfs2_ail_flush_reqd(sdp) ||
  				gfs2_jrnl_flush_reqd(sdp) ||
  				sdp->sd_log_error ||
* Unmerged path fs/gfs2/log.c
diff --git a/fs/gfs2/quota.c b/fs/gfs2/quota.c
index 6caaa00aaf67..8dd84990eec0 100644
--- a/fs/gfs2/quota.c
+++ b/fs/gfs2/quota.c
@@ -1594,11 +1594,9 @@ int gfs2_quotad(void *data)
 		quotad_check_timeo(sdp, "sync", gfs2_quota_sync, t,
 				   &quotad_timeo, &tune->gt_quota_quantum);
 
-		try_to_freeze();
-
 		t = min(quotad_timeo, statfs_timeo);
 
-		t = wait_event_interruptible_timeout(sdp->sd_quota_wait,
+		t = wait_event_freezable_timeout(sdp->sd_quota_wait,
 				sdp->sd_statfs_force_sync ||
 				gfs2_withdrawn(sdp) ||
 				kthread_should_stop(),
